From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wolf Vollprecht <w.vollprecht@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 16:20:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] foundationpose_models_install: register the asset script
 without running it at build time

NOT an upstream fix -- a packaging deviation, deliberately. `install_isaac_ros_asset`
lives in isaac_ros_common, whose cmake/ directory is under NVIDIA's proprietary header,
so the fix cannot be made where the problem is. See ISSUES.md.

`install_isaac_ros_asset(install_foundationpose_models)` does two things that a package
build cannot do, and the first one is what fails:

  1. It `execute_process`es the install script with `--print-install-paths` at configure
     time. The script derives every path from `$ISAAC_ROS_WS`, so with that variable
     unset -- which it is in any environment that is not NVIDIA's dev container --
     isaac_ros_common-extras-assets.cmake aborts with

         ERROR: ISAAC_ROS_WS is not set.

  2. It then hangs the script off `add_custom_target(... ALL)`, making the default build
     target download refine_model.onnx and score_model.onnx from NGC (behind a EULA
     prompt) and run `trtexec` over both to produce .plan files.

Step 2 is not something to work around -- it is something not to do. A TensorRT engine
plan is specialised to the GPU, driver and TensorRT version it was built with, so a plan
baked into a binary package is wrong for every machine except the builder's. The models
belong on the target system, which is also how NVIDIA documents installing them:

    ros2 run isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install install_foundationpose_models.sh

So keep the two things that make that command work -- the script in `lib/<pkg>/` (which
the untouched `install(PROGRAMS ...)` below already does) and the ament resource pointing
at it -- and drop the build-time download. The resource is registered with exactly the
name, content and install path `install_isaac_ros_asset` would have used, so
`get_isaac_ros_asset_install_script_path()` resolves identically for consumers.
---
 isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install/CMakeLists.txt | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install/CMakeLists.txt b/isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -19,7 +19,15 @@ project(isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install)
 find_package(ament_cmake_auto REQUIRED)
 ament_auto_find_build_dependencies()

-install_isaac_ros_asset(install_foundationpose_models)
+# Was install_isaac_ros_asset(install_foundationpose_models), which dry-runs the script
+# at configure time (needs $ISAAC_ROS_WS) and then downloads the ONNX models and runs
+# trtexec as part of `ALL`. Neither can happen in a binary package build, and the engine
+# plans would be wrong for every GPU but the builder's anyway. Register the resource the
+# way that function would have, and leave the download to the target system:
+#   ros2 run isaac_ros_foundationpose_models_install install_foundationpose_models.sh
+ament_index_register_resource("install_foundationpose_models"
+  CONTENT
+  "${CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX}/lib/${PROJECT_NAME}/install_foundationpose_models.sh")
 install(PROGRAMS asset_scripts/install_foundationpose_models.sh DESTINATION lib/${PROJECT_NAME})

 # Embed versioning information into installed files
